  "worked_solution": "We can use the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta -{sin}^{2}\u2061\\theta =\\operatorname{cos}\u20612\\theta \n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (3{x}^{2}-{sin}^{2}\u2061x+{cos}^{2}\u2061x)\\text{d}x & =\\int (3{x}^{2}+{cos}^{2}\u2061x-{sin}^{2}\u2061x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (3{x}^{2}+\\operatorname{cos}\u20612x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3(\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3})+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}\u20612x+C \\\\  & ={x}^{3}+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}\u20612x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
